diff --git a/NOTICE b/NOTICE
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..9c0fb33
--- /dev/null
+++ b/NOTICE
@@ -0,0 +1,24 @@
+This is the Runink fork of DEsk.
+
+DEsk is by fyzugx and the DEsk authors: https://github.com/fyzugx/DEsk
+(MIT License, LICENSE). The fork follows upstream's releases and carries a
+short series of changes on top of them; each one that suits upstream is
+offered there.
+
+What the fork changes (`git log upstream/main..`):
+
+- The build runs no Python: tools/glsl2c.c and tools/room-key.c, built by
+  the build itself, replace scripts/glsl2c.py and scripts/room-key.py, and
+  tools/checkwords (Go) replaces scripts/check-words.py. The icon generator
+  scripts are not carried; the SVGs they drew are. art/looks/bake.py and
+  art/kit.py (Blender scripts, for desk-look bake) are not installed.
+- It runs on systems without systemd: sd-bus from libelogind, --systemd and
+  systemctl only where systemd is init, loginctl for powering off.
+- -Dweather_default=false builds a desk that asks the network nothing until
+  its user turns the weather on.
+- Shell Settings' Bluetooth and Printers rows, and the Control Panel's
+  Bluetooth lever, also open river-bluetooth and river-printers (where
+  blueman and system-config-printer, which are Python, are not carried).
+
+Nothing upstream wrote has been relicensed; the fork's own changes are under
+the same MIT License, as "The RIVER Authors".
diff --git a/README.md b/README.md
index 62582b8..0f81185 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -2,6 +2,9 @@
 
 # DEsk
 
+> This is the **Runink fork** of DEsk, by fyzugx and the DEsk authors
+> ([upstream](https://github.com/fyzugx/DEsk)). What it changes is in [NOTICE](NOTICE).
+
 **v0.2.1 (BETA)** -- fixes for v0.2: the Control Panel's key and lid on a slower machine and on a touch screen, the top edge of the opened lid, and the drawer's sounds in time with the drawer. v0.2 brought new things to the desk: a calculator, one notebook to type and write in, Print as a camera that also films, and picture-in-picture as an old phone; touch, an on-screen typewriter, a pen and handwriting, and a screen that turns with the machine; the Control Panel redesigned in four; woods, stains and desk mats; favourites, a clipboard and looks for the drawer. See [RELEASE-NOTES.md](RELEASE-NOTES.md).
 
 Homepage: https://fyzugx.github.io/DEsk/ -- the highlights, a desk you can try in your browser, the install steps and an FAQ.
